    "title": "Concept: What are Abiotic Factors?",
    "explanation": "<p class=\"text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground\">Abiotic factors are the <strong>non-living</strong> parts of an ecosystem that influence where organisms can live and how well they survive. Examples include <em>temperature, light intensity, moisture levels, soil pH, wind intensity, and carbon dioxide concentrations</em>. These factors affect both the <strong>distribution</strong> (where organisms are found) and <strong>abundance</strong> (how many organisms live there) of species.</p>",
